{"ts": "2026-10-16T15:09:58.499740Z", "run_id": "r-20261016T1442Z-fd5b", "unit": "openspec:add-telemetry-runtime", "seq": 49, "type": "task.red_ok", "task": "6.1", "base": "f55a6bae7af17b75c490eb55709f5622568cb587", "tests": ["packages.core.tests.test_telemetry_resource_sampling::test_context_propagates_by_default", "packages.core.tests.test_telemetry_resource_sampling::test_otel_service_name_wins_and_resource_attributes_override_namespace", "packages.core.tests.test_telemetry_resource_sampling::test_resource_attribute_service_name_wins_without_otel_service_name", "packages.core.tests.test_telemetry_resource_sampling::test_resource_uses_the_callers_default_service_name", "packages.core.tests.test_telemetry_resource_sampling::test_sampler_always_off_exports_nothing_while_the_default_exports"], "frozen": [], "notes": "tdd_exemption: the four criteria were made true by 7ceb3e1 (task 4.1) and are already satisfied at HEAD. The five new tests pass at HEAD (full gate: 1655 passed, 114 skipped, coverage 91%) and each FAILS BY ASSERTION against the unit base, verified with a full-suite base swap of telemetry.py+config.py to 7942c55 (junit lists all five as AssertionError 'init_telemetry is missing the test seam'). So the base run confirms all four criteria. The Python zero-value run aborts collection (zeroing public telemetry.traced breaks storage.py import), exactly as for tasks 4.4/5.1/5.2, so the base run is the proof. Each test asserts real values (service.name, service.version, namespace, deployment.environment.name, trace/span ids, a real 'kept' span) and, where the expected answer is empty (sampling off), also asserts a positive control in the same test. Accepted findings: F-1619b9 (one WARNING per bad shared variable; OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL checked once) belongs to task 4.1, untouched. F-0ad188 (_Scrubbing keeps _inner) belongs to 4b.2/7.1, untouched. F-fea82d (comma-list exporter semantics; _service_name/_resolve_state/_traces_endpoint signatures): no scenario